      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T22:33:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e James: The pointer arithmetic here seems wrong. `ref_stride` should only be used after `ref8` is converted back to `SHORTPTR`.\n\n`CONVERT_TO_SHORTPTR` doubles the value, then the stride is added to a `uint16_t`, doubling the effect. Converting it back would halve it, no?\n\nDoes this path get hit by any tests?",
      "parentUuid": "582b92e3_e3ac7b90",
      "revId": "0006e96cdb595ff88950a2c664115335ca5517bf",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
